A||||3||GarethWright||Where is the Body Number Plate?||||5||
Z||000000||GarethWright||04-03-2001||02:05 AM||||see title  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Haynes says "the body number plate is located in the front compartment attached to the front tie bar behind either the left or right headlamp" but what is a Tie Bar? Am I looking for a sticker or a stamped metal plate or what? By the looks of the Haynes drawing of it, it could be riveted somewhere.  Any idea where I can get a listing of all the original options that the factory put on the car?<BR>Thanks<BR>Gareth||||reg||5
Z||000001||Wolfhound||04-03-2001||06:15 AM||||If you open the front compartment there is a approx 3X5 white sticker with the option codes on it, on top of the drivers side wheel well. I believe the VIN is in several locations on the car beside the one visible in the windshield. One I know of is below the drivers side dash speaker, if it is removed. 87-88 fieros had vinyl stick on VIN,s on most ever body panel even under the tag.<BR>Coy<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||GarethWright||04-03-2001||02:31 PM||||Oh ok, so it IS that sticker, Thats the only one I saw in there, but it doesn't looks much like the pic in the haynes manual.  Is there anyplace I can go to find the meanings of the codes?<BR>thanks again<BR>Gareth||||reg||1
Z||000003||Wolfhound||04-03-2001||04:13 PM||||These are called RPO Codes and are used in production. Here is one site identifying them.<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/techtips.htm#RPOCodes" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/techtips.htm#RPOCodes</A> <P>Scroll down to RPO Codes.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 04-03-2001).]||||reg||1
